:: Carter Bedroom Play Sword Dual [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>
As the two of you are deciding what to play, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> suddenly picks up a foam sword and points it at you! <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Ready yourself, villain! For today is the day you are slain!”</span> He proclaims as you put your hands up, smirking. You ask him if it is really heroic to slay someone who can’t defend himself and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> quickly responds <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Of course not!”</span> He then tosses you the sword in his hand and picks up the other one. <span style="color:LightGreen">Suddenly, the two of you are readying yourself for a dual to the death! Or, at least, until one of you admits defeat.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Smirk",
                Eyes: "Mad",
            },	
        },
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Smirk",
                Eyes: "Mad",
            },	
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Take this!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> lunges at you swiftly, his small body making him light on his feet. You just barely manage to jump back and respond with a swish of your own, but your small friend easily parries it, stabbing towards you and nipping your shirt! You gasp as you jump back again. <span style="color:Yellow"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s quick, a little too quick, and he seems right at home with a blade in hand. He’s probably trained with the sword more times than you can count, against all sorts of imaginary adversaries, even some real ones. Larger ones, like his brother or father, you’d imagine. This gives him not only the confidence, but the skill as he needs to keep you on the defensive. But very soon you run out of ground behind you, finding yourself pinned against the wall as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s doesn’t even seem to be breaking a sweat!</span> <br>
<br>
You don’t see a way forward outside of admitting defeat or falling on the sword, at least, <span style="color:Pink">not until you spy the shining silver of the button on <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s $CarterBottoms.Type. It looks loose, barely holding itself together. This may be your one chance-</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
    <<link "Admit defeat<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        But it’s a long shot, and probably one <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> may find a bit embarrassing, so for one reason or another you drop your sword and lift your hands into the air, surrendering. You bow down and admit <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is the finer swordsman, so you admit defeat at his hands. <span style="color:LightGreen"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> smiles proudly at this, keeping his sword trained on you until he knocks yours away, probably suspecting some sort of trick.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Good.”</span> He chuckles, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Well, since you admitted defeat, I suppose I shall let you live this time, villain, but only if you swear to toss aside villainy and only fight on the side of justice from now on!”</span> You agree, though request that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, the master swordsman, trains you in some of his moves. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I suppose I can do that, though only some, since I still don’t trust that you won’t return to your old evil ways!”</span> <br>
        <br>
        The rest of the game is spent with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> showing off his moves and techniques, which you quickly learn are just things he saw on TV that he trained enough times to master. <span style="color:LightGreen">It is a little crazy how good <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is with the foam sword and how much control he seems to have over it. You wonder if he’ll end up joining the fencing team in high school.</span> <br>

        <span style="color:Green">+Carter Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
        <span style="color:red">-Carter Energy</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Energy -= 10>>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
        <<socialChange "Carter" 1>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Carter House Carter Bedroom]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<link "Swing for his shorts<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        With a smile, you fake a swing towards <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s head, a dangerous and precise maneuver. <span style="color:LightGreen">But luckily, he falls for it, raising his own blade into the sky to parry! Everything seems to move in slow motions as you whip your sword around, avoiding his head and chest where he was already set to block, and swish down towards his waist!</span> <span style="color:Pink">You only barely hit his button and with just enough force to do what you planned. <br>
        <br>
        Pop! <br>
        <br>
        The button pops open with an audible click! <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> stumbles back in surprise as you begin to hit him with a flurry of blows of your own, causing his body to shake and bounce around enough to loosen his bottoms more and more as a panicked <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> realizes what is happening but has no chance to stop it! <br>
 
            <<set _ad to [
